/*
===========================================
CHANGE-OVER-TIME ANALYSIS
===========================================

Purpose:
Analyze how key business measures evolve over time. This type of analysis helps
identify trends, seasonality, growth patterns, and changes in customer behavior.

What this query does:
1. Aggregates sales data by year and month.
2. Calculates total sales, total customers, and total quantity for each period.
3. Produces a time-series view that supports trend analysis and seasonal insights.

Key Concepts:
- Date-based aggregation (year, month)
- Trend and seasonality detection
- Business KPI tracking over time

Tables used:
- gold.fact_sales

===========================================
*/

-- Change-Over-Time Analysis
-- Aggregates key business metrics by year and month to identify trends and seasonality.

SELECT
    EXTRACT(YEAR FROM order_date::date) AS order_year,
    EXTRACT(MONTH FROM order_date::date) AS order_month,
    SUM(sales_amount) AS total_sales,
    COUNT(DISTINCT customer_key) AS total_customers,
    SUM(quantity) AS total_quantity
FROM gold.fact_sales
WHERE order_date IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY
    EXTRACT(YEAR FROM order_date::date),
    EXTRACT(MONTH FROM order_date::date)
ORDER BY
    order_year,
    order_month;
